From 82f12852b49b2a698dffbf7faaac17fbef916adc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Release Radar <release-radar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:33:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Home-network address: use the LAN when it answers, the
 tunnel otherwise

The server connection config keeps its address as the server's identity
(config id, tokens, downloads, progress). An optional second address for
the home network is only a route: a native ServerRoute object probes it
(healthcheck, /status is Audiobookshelf with our version, /api/me with our
token returns our own user id) on every network change, and an OkHttp
interceptor on the shared client rewrites API, stream and download
requests to it while it answers, retrying GET/HEAD once on the canonical
address when it fails to connect. The JS layer follows the same route for
its own requests and covers, with one retry. The live socket stays on the
canonical address. New field on the account page; the stream rides out a
switch with a more patient load-error policy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

